WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.554
Step seven.

00:00:00.604 --> 00:00:04.891
A change goes to production the way a team would ship it: branch, pull request,

00:00:04.941 --> 00:00:06.648
checks, review, merge, approval.

00:00:06.698 --> 00:00:09.389
Pull request four changes one paragraph of the portal.

00:00:09.439 --> 00:00:13.196
The template asks what changed, how it was tested, and how to roll it back.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:16.922
The files changed tab shows the exact diff the reviewer approves.

00:00:16.972 --> 00:00:20.151
It merged only after the checks passed: twelve checks,

00:00:20.201 --> 00:00:22.662
including the eleven the ruleset requires.

00:00:22.712 --> 00:00:24.522
The merge started the app workflow.

00:00:24.572 --> 00:00:26.807
After approval, the new version rolled out.

00:00:26.857 --> 00:00:29.183
And it is live: the new sentence is there,

00:00:29.233 --> 00:00:31.786
and the version badge shows the merged commit.

00:00:32.836 --> 00:00:37.049
Pull request five changes infrastructure: the autoscaler maximum goes from four to

00:00:37.099 --> 00:00:37.309
five.

00:00:37.359 --> 00:00:40.116
The what-if job runs with the pull-request credential.

00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:42.235
Its comment lists what would change.

00:00:42.285 --> 00:00:44.472
The cluster shows Modify, as expected.

00:00:44.522 --> 00:00:48.710
Some other rows are what-if noise, so read the details before you merge.
